> ### Q4: "needs visa" border check (must-fail case #6) — which validator owns this?
> None of the four SPEC validators (connectivity, opening_hours, geography, budget) naturally handle visa requirements. Options:
> - Treat it as a **connectivity** violation (no valid GTFS trip across a border requiring a visa)
> - Exclude it from the four-validator scope and mark it as a known limitation
> - Add a fifth lightweight validator
>
> Recommendation: model it as a connectivity failure — "no transit leg exists between Prague and a non-Schengen city" — since the GTFS feed simply won't contain that route.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> ### Q5: "Overlapping activities" (must-fail case #10) — which validator?
> Two activities at the same time slot could be caught by `geography` (can't be in two places) or `opening_hours` (time conflict). Recommendation: treat as `geography` — "zero travel time between two distinct coordinates at overlapping times is physically impossible."

